  "description": "Numeric spanning forest; requires >>uf. _mst<T=ll> uses T directly for edge costs and ret() (ll, i128 and ld are supported). add(u,v,cost) returns a stable zero-based edge ID. build(components=1,maximum=false) recomputes the minimum forest by default, or maximum when true, stopping at the requested component count when reachable. It returns false if disconnected input prevents the target; ret() and it_edge() then expose the maximum-cardinality forest produced. Equal costs are ordered by insertion ID in both modes. ret() returns the cached scalar total; it_edge(f) calls f(id,u,v,cost) on selected original edges in selection order. Integer costs accumulate in i128 before conversion to T; intermediate sums must fit i128 and the final total must fit T. Floating totals accumulate in T. Rebuild after adding input, and clear(n,base=1) resets inputs and IDs. Vertex n is the maximum external index. Build is O(n+m log m), ret O(1), and edge iteration O(selected edges)."
